Existing behaviour, pinned by t/58-import-next-id-seed.t, surfaced by the #60 work.

The counter lives in refs/karr/meta/next-id. `karr materialize` now writes
next_id into the view as well, because kanban-md validates it and refuses a file
without it (#60). But `karr import` deliberately ignores the file's copy and
seeds the counter from the highest task id it sees instead.

That is safe as long as the view only ever loses tasks. It is not safe when
kanban-md advanced the counter past the highest id — which it does whenever a
task is created and then deleted in a kanban-md session. karr then re-seeds
below kanban-md's counter, and the next `karr create` hands out an id that
kanban-md considers already used.

Note this is not the #44 race, which is fixed. This is the two tools
disagreeing about the counter across a bridge crossing.

Fix direction: seed from max(highest task id + 1, next_id from the view), so
the counter can move forward across the bridge but never backwards. The
existing test pins the current behaviour, so it has to be updated deliberately
rather than worked around.
